    <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-360" contextRef="c-03">&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;1.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;2.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;3.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;4.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 14pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 10pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;5.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="width: 10.44pt; font: 7pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;; display: inline-block"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: &amp;quot;Segoe UI&amp;quot;"&gt;N/A&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-362" contextRef="c-03">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 10pt"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;The Company&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Mid-America Pipeline Company, LLC (&amp;quot;Mid-America&amp;quot;) is a Texas limited liability company and a wholly owned subsidiary of Mapletree, LLC, a Delaware limited liability company. Mapletree, LLC is a wholly owned subsidiary of Enterprise Products Operating LLC (EPOLLC), a Texas limited liability company. EPOLLC in turn is wholly owned by Enterprise Products Partners L.P., a Delaware limited partnership, which is a publicly traded partnership. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;EPOLLC is the operator of the Mid-America pipeline system.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Description of the Property&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Mid-America owns a natural gas liquids (&amp;quot;NGL&amp;quot;) pipeline system that is approximately 7,830 miles in length. It consists of three primary systems: the approximately 3,000-mile Rocky Mountain System, the approximately 2,800-mile Northern system and the approximately 2,030-mile Central System. Mid-America's operations cover thirteen states: Wyoming, Utah, Colorado, New Mexico, Texas, Oklahoma, Kansas, Missouri, Nebraska, Iowa, Illinois, Minnesota, and Wisconsin. The Rocky Mountain System transports mixed natural gas liquids from the Rocky Mountain Overthrust and San Juan Basin areas to the Hobbs hub, located on the Texas/New Mexico border. The Northern system links the NGL hub at Conway, Kansas to refineries, petrochemical plants, and propane markets in the upper Midwest. The Central System connects the Conway hub with Kansas refineries and transports NGLs between Conway, Kansas, and the Hobbs Hub.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; Starting in January 2024, Mid-America leased certain pipeline capacity to its affiliate, Enterprise TW Products Pipeline Company, LLC, for refined products transportation service originating in Hobbs, Texas and delivering to terminal locations in New Mexico, and Utah.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements conform to those required by FERC. Financial statements are prepared on the accrual basis of accounting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; Property, plant and equipment assets are recorded at original cost.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Mid-America's revenues are primarily derived from transportation of natural gas liquids under intrastate and interstate tariffs. The tariffs specify the amounts to be paid by shippers for service between receipt and delivery locations and the general terms and conditions of transportation services on the pipeline system. Revenues are recognized upon delivery of products to customers.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;During 2025, Mid-America rebilled shippers for under-recovery resulting from the vacated January 20, 2022 rehearing order (Docket No. RM20-14-001) in the amount of $5,973,167.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; (See Commission's order issued on November 20, 2025 (Docket No. RM93-11-003, paragraph 37, footnote 111)).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt; These revenues are reported in account 645 &amp;quot;Unusual or Infrequent Items (credit)&amp;quot; on page 114.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Mid-America is a limited liability company that passes income tax liability through the company to EPOLLC and, with the exception of the Texas Franchise Tax, if applicable, does not recognize this liability on Mid-America's financial statements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;For purposes of calculating income taxes for the annual cost of service (shown on page 700 of the Annual Report), Mid-America employs FERC's Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-weight: bold"&gt;Employees&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt"&gt; 				&lt;span&gt;Mid-America has no employees of its own. All operations, management, and administrative functions are performed by employees of Enterprise Products Company on behalf of EPOLLC, the operator.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;Mid-America reimburses EPOLLC for management and administrative functions under the terms of an operating agreement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
